# Ancient Cornucopia: "Do this only once each turn." Bot1 casts a Lightning Bolt and, while that cast's trigger is still on the
# stack, a second Lightning Bolt: both triggered (Bot1 had gained no life when each was cast, CR 603.2h). The second trigger,
# on top, resolves first and Bot1 accepts, gaining 1. When the first trigger then resolves the action has been done this
# turn, so it does nothing and Bot1 is not asked (the refusal): the life gain happens once, 20 + 1 = 21.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ancient Cornucopia
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancient Cornucopia.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Cornucopia.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Stack.Count = 4
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
